The `/api/me` function makes a request to `https://api.github.com/user` with the token as a Bearer token. If the GitHub API returns an error, `!res.ok` would be true, and the function returns `{ authed: false }`.

The most likely reason for the GitHub API to fail is an invalid or expired token. But the token was just obtained from the OAuth flow.

