Now I see the actual issue! The GitHub API is returning 403 with:

```
Request forbidden by administrative rules. Please make sure your request has a User-Agent header
```

GitHub's API requires a `User-Agent` header to be set. Looking at the `/api/me` code:

```js
const res = await fetch('https://api.github.com/user', {
  headers: {
    'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`,
    'Accept': 'application/vnd.github+json'
  }
});
```

There's no `User-Agent` header! GitHub's API requires a `User-Agent` header in every request. Without it, the request is rejected with a 403 error.

The fix is simple: add a `User-Agent` header to the request. This is a well-known requirement of the GitHub API.

Let me fix `/api/me` to include a User-Agent header.

