footer{ margin-top:4rem; padding-top:2rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.2); font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); }
```

No table styles! Tables would render with default browser styling which is quite ugly. Let me test this theory by checking if the HTML output has the `<table>` tag but it looks bad in the browser.

The issue is likely that the Markdown-to-HTML conversion IS working (producing `<table>` HTML), but the CSS doesn't style tables, so they look broken.

